      "hints": [
        "Calculate $m_{AB} = \\frac{2 - 0}{0 - 4} = -\\frac{1}{2}$.",
        "Set perpendicular gradient $m_{BC} = 2 = \\frac{3h - 2}{h - 0}$ and solve for $h$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Calculate the gradient of line segment $AB$ connecting $A(4, 0)$ and $B(0, 2)$:\n$$m_{AB} = \\frac{2 - 0}{0 - 4} = -\\frac{2}{4} = -\\frac{1}{2}$$",
        "Since $\\angle ABC = 90^\\circ$, line $BC$ is perpendicular to $AB$:\n$$m_{BC} = -\\frac{1}{-1/2} = 2$$",
        "Set the gradient of $BC$ through $B(0, 2)$ and $C(h, 3h)$ equal to $2$:\n$$\\frac{3h - 2}{h - 0} = 2 \\implies 3h - 2 = 2h \\implies h = 2$$"
      ],
